---
description: Run the start-session workspace scan at the beginning of every new session
alwaysApply: true
---

At the start of a new session in this repo, run the `start-session` skill
(see `.github/skills/start-session/SKILL.md`) before doing anything else —
don't wait to be asked.

1. **Last-run check first.** Read `.claude/skills/start-session/.last-run.json`
   (create if absent; treat missing as "never run"). If `lastRunUtc` is the
   same calendar day (local time), skip the full scan and note
   "start-session already ran today at `<time>`" — don't re-scan git. **Still
   list active ADO PRs targeting `main`** (`create-prs.ps1 -ListActive`).
   Otherwise run the full scan and write the updated timestamp back at the
   end. This file is per-repo, per-machine state — never commit it.

2. **Installed-agent drift check.** If a `cp-ai-toolkit` checkout is findable
   in this workspace (sibling folder, or `C:\devops\cp-ai-toolkit`), run its
   `scripts/start-session/Compare-InstalledAgents.ps1` (read-only) against
   this repo. Report any stale/missing shared agent or skill files and
   suggest re-running `Install-CPAIAgents.ps1` — don't run it automatically.
   Skip silently if no toolkit checkout is found.

3. Then follow the full behavior in `.github/skills/start-session/SKILL.md`:
   discovery (git status/log per workspace repo), ADO remote query via
   `@admin-ado`, and policy-gated PR surfacing (never auto-merge, never push
   a local-only branch without explicit approval).
